SUMMARY:Strawberry Gap
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n[https://maps.app.goo.gl/v6bUg7qyx
 qX4PDuo8](https://maps.app.goo.gl/v6bUg7qyxqX4PDuo8)\n\n5 miles\, approx 1
 100 ft elevation gain. see link below to AllTrails\n\npace of 2 - 2.5 mph\
 n\nsorry no dogs are allowed on this trail as it passes through private pr
 operty\n\nStrawberry Gap Trail on AllTrails\n[https://www.alltrails.com/tr
 ail/us/north-carolina/strawberry-gap-trail?sh=pacpnj&utm_medium=trail_shar
 e&utm_source=alltrails_virality](https://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/north-
 carolina/strawberry-gap-trail?sh=pacpnj&utm_medium=trail_share&utm_source=
 alltrails_virality)\n\nper previous hikes:\n\ngear up as appropriate\, tre
 kking poles are an option. bring a snack as we'll take a break mid-hike. a
 nd plenty of water\n\nground rules: 1) if you sign up\, show up or change 
 your status. 2 ) be sure you are in adequate physical shape to complete th
 e event. 3) show consideration toward all attendees. I hike for stress red
 uction and want to keep it that way as much as possible\n\n**LEGALESE**\nT
 his Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transpor
 tation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their
  own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical co
 nditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself
  and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can 
 assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for this event\,
  participant understands and agrees
